{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This structure captures ~20% of a complete D96A EANCOM INVOIC ontology. Critical gaps include: no monetary amounts (MOA), no dates (DTM), no quantities (QTY), no line-level pricing (PRI), no tax details (TAX), no references (RFF), no allowances/charges (ALC), and no totals validation segments. The current model cannot represent a legally compliant invoice.",
  "completeness_score": 0.22,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "DTM_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Document Date (DTM+137) is MANDATORY in EANCOM INVOIC. Without this, the invoice has no legal date of issue. Must support qualifiers: 137 (Document), 35 (Delivery), 11 (Despatch), 263 (Invoice Period Start), 264 (Invoice Period End)."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 4}

{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "Your model now covers approximately 60-65% of a D96A EANCOM INVOIC message. While you have added critical transactional segments (DTM, MOA, QTY, PRI, TAX, RFF, ALC), you are missing mandatory structural components (UNH/UNT message envelope, LIN line item identifier), critical detail segments (IMD item description, PIA additional product IDs, PAC packaging), and essential party/logistics segments (CUX currency, TOD terms of delivery, LOC location). A complete D96A INVOIC ontology requires 15-20 segment types minimum.",
  "completeness_score": 0.63,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "UNH_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "MANDATORY. Message Header segment - defines message type (INVOIC), version (D), release (96A), controlling agency (UN), association code (EAN008 for EANCOM). Without", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 3}

{"expert_response": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "The ontology has improved significantly with 21 segment types now modeled. However, critical gaps remain for D96A EANCOM INVOIC compliance. You are missing mandatory segments for allowances/charges detail (ALC sub-structure), references at line level, dates at line level, and crucially the FTX (Free Text) segment which is mandatory for certain invoice types. Structural coverage is approximately 70-75%, but semantic completeness requires additional constraints and composite element modeling.",

  "completeness_score": 0.72,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "FTX_Segment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Free Text (FTX) is MANDATORY in D96A EANCOM for invoice notes, payment terms descriptions, and legal text. Qualifier 4451 distinguishes between AAI (general information), PMT (payment terms), REG (regulatory information). Without FTX, you cannot represent human-readable invoice annotations required by EN 16931", "consultation_logged": true, "calls_remaining": 2}

